      "id": 14361,
      "name": "pwatson1974",
      "username": "pwatson1974",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/pwatson1974/{size}/1925_2.png",
      "created_at": "2016-02-03T12:07:20.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Something I was thinking about while compiling all the start screen texts.</p><p>How will the promos be distributed across the remaining updates for Handelabra. Below are my thoughts.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Minipack 3 (Guise, Wager Master, Omnitron IV)</p><p>Promos:</p><p>Santa Guise, following the Scholar's pattern of introducing the promo with the minipack character.</p><p>Chrono-Ranger: The Best of Times, because frankly there isn't anyone else available at that point. I'm not sure Omnitron-U will be in existence when this gets created and the others are all part of defined groups which Handelabra quite reasonably seem to want to keep together for thematic reasons.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Wrath of the Cosmos</p><p>Promos:</p><p>The Prime Wardens (Argent Adept, Captain Cosmic, Fanatic, Haka, Tempest): This one seems obvious It's a big team of promos to distribute and until Cosmic arrives, there isn't much point to doing so.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Season 2</p><p>Vengeance</p><p>Promos:</p><p>KNYFE: Rogue Agent, Hunted Naturalist, Dark Watch Setback, Adamant Sentinels: Mostly this is just because these are available now and Handelabra probably want to release more promos with the larger packages.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Minipack 4 (Chokepoint, Celestial Tribunal)</p><p>Promos:</p><p>Termi-Nation (Absolute Zero, Bunker, Unity). With Chokepoint being introduced, it seems aposite to introduce her nemeses' promos.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Villains of the Multiverse:</p><p>Promos:</p><p>Heroic Infinitor, Trickster Kismet: What better point to add the last two villain promos than in the expansion that's all about the villains?</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>OblivAeon:</p><p>Promos:</p><p>Omnitron-U, unrevealed Parse promo, unrevealed Sky-Scraper promo: Just to clear up the list. If lots of promos are associated with OblivAeon, as is entirely possible, these may be moved to another set.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Unknown:</p><p>Kvorthe Sixstring Argent Adept: Given his status as a charity reward promo, I'm somewhat doubtful he'll appear in the video game. If so, no idea which set is most appropriate for him.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Antyone have any thoughts?</p>",
